<div class="color-scheme-2 gradient">
  <div class="page-width section-template--24127198429470__faq-padding"><div class="faq-content isolate content-container content-container--full-width">
      <div class="faq-content__wrapper faq-with-content__block">
        
          <div class="faq-content-wrapper__inner">
            
              <div class="faq-section__content sp-small"><div class="subheading__text rte">
                    <p><strong>LEARN MORE</strong></p>
                  </div>
                  <h2
                    class="faq-block__heading inline-richtext h2"
                    
                  >
                    FAQ's
                  </h2>
                  <div class="faq-block__description rte" >
                    <p>Also find us on social media.</p>
                  </div>
                
</div>
            
            
          </div>
        
        <div class="faq-content__grid">
          <vertical-slider class="faqs-verticle-slider top-to-bottom faq-hidden__overlay">
            <div class="faq-accordions"><div class="faq-accordion-item auto-scrolling-height">
                  <button type="button" class="h5 accordion-toggle-btn" data-toggle="#accordion-toggle-content-faq_1">
                    Who are Beginner Sessions for? 
                    <span class="toggle-svg button--primary">
                      
    <svg
      class="svg-icon icon-plus"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="14"
      height="14"
      viewBox="0 0 14 14"
      fill="none"
      style="--width: 14px;"
    >
      <path d="M7.21191 2.18994V12.5839" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M2.01562 7.38696H12.4096" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  

                    </span>
                  </button>
                  <div id="accordion-toggle-content-faq_1" class="accordion-toggle-content">
                    <div class="faq-block__details-content rte">
                      <p>Perfect for pickle newbies or those dusting off their skills. Come as you are, learn in a laid-back setting, and discover why everyone's obsessed with this game!</p><h3></h3>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div><div class="faq-accordion-item auto-scrolling-height">
                  <button type="button" class="h5 accordion-toggle-btn" data-toggle="#accordion-toggle-content-faq_J3Kmkj">
                    Who should join All Skills or Advanced Beginner Sessions 
                    <span class="toggle-svg button--primary">
                      
    <svg
      class="svg-icon icon-plus"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="14"
      height="14"
      viewBox="0 0 14 14"
      fill="none"
      style="--width: 14px;"
    >
      <path d="M7.21191 2.18994V12.5839" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M2.01562 7.38696H12.4096" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  

                    </span>
                  </button>
                  <div id="accordion-toggle-content-faq_J3Kmkj" class="accordion-toggle-content">
                    <div class="faq-block__details-content rte">
                      <p>Got the basics down? These sessions keep the social vibes high while helping you level up your game. We play actual matches, so knowing scoring and basic rules is key. Focus on upping your consistency, placement, and court flow in our friendly match format.</p><p>💡 <strong>New to the paddle life?</strong> Start with our Beginner Sessions or Coaching Programs!</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div><div class="faq-accordion-item auto-scrolling-height">
                  <button type="button" class="h5 accordion-toggle-btn" data-toggle="#accordion-toggle-content-faq_qdFE8P">
                    Who should join Intermediate or Advanced Sessions 
                    <span class="toggle-svg button--primary">
                      
    <svg
      class="svg-icon icon-plus"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="14"
      height="14"
      viewBox="0 0 14 14"
      fill="none"
      style="--width: 14px;"
    >
      <path d="M7.21191 2.18994V12.5839" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M2.01562 7.38696H12.4096" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  

                    </span>
                  </button>
                  <div id="accordion-toggle-content-faq_qdFE8P" class="accordion-toggle-content">
                    <div class="faq-block__details-content rte">
                      <p>Social Intermediate games are for experienced players. Please do not join this session unless you are an intermediate level.</p><p>Advanced and Intermediate games are for experienced players. Please do not join this session unless you are an intermediate/advanced level. If you are unsure, join an Advanced Beginner or All Skills Session first and speak to the organisers about the session most suitable to your skill level</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div><div class="faq-accordion-item auto-scrolling-height">
                  <button type="button" class="h5 accordion-toggle-btn" data-toggle="#accordion-toggle-content-faq_2">
                    How do social pickleball sessions work at  Pickle &amp;? 
                    <span class="toggle-svg button--primary">
                      
    <svg
      class="svg-icon icon-plus"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="14"
      height="14"
      viewBox="0 0 14 14"
      fill="none"
      style="--width: 14px;"
    >
      <path d="M7.21191 2.18994V12.5839" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M2.01562 7.38696H12.4096" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  

                    </span>
                  </button>
                  <div id="accordion-toggle-content-faq_2" class="accordion-toggle-content">
                    <div class="faq-block__details-content rte">
                      <p>Our pickleball sessions are primarily focused on doubles play, offering a fun and engaging way to interact and compete. Players rotate allowing everyone the opportunity to play with different partners and against various opponents. This rotation ensures a lively and varied experience for all participants.</p><p>Our game host is there to facilitate smooth rotations and to help match players of similar skill levels, ensuring a balanced and enjoyable game for everyone.</p><p>Please note, there is no official break within the session, but players are encouraged to take short breaks for rest or hydration as needed. The sessions are designed to be player-friendly, allowing for flexibility and comfort.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div><div class="faq-accordion-item auto-scrolling-height">
                  <button type="button" class="h5 accordion-toggle-btn" data-toggle="#accordion-toggle-content-faq_3">
                    What should I wear? 
                    <span class="toggle-svg button--primary">
                      
    <svg
      class="svg-icon icon-plus"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="14"
      height="14"
      viewBox="0 0 14 14"
      fill="none"
      style="--width: 14px;"
    >
      <path d="M7.21191 2.18994V12.5839" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M2.01562 7.38696H12.4096" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  

                    </span>
                  </button>
                  <div id="accordion-toggle-content-faq_3" class="accordion-toggle-content">
                    <div class="faq-block__details-content rte">
                      <p>Comfy athletic gear that lets you move, non-marking court shoes with good grip, and moisture-wicking socks. For outdoor sessions, don't forget sun protection!</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div><div class="faq-accordion-item">
                  <button type="button" class="h5 accordion-toggle-btn" data-toggle="#accordion-toggle-content-faq_4">
                    What is the cancellation and no-show policy for pickleball sessions? 
                    <span class="toggle-svg button--primary">
                      
    <svg
      class="svg-icon icon-plus"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="14"
      height="14"
      viewBox="0 0 14 14"
      fill="none"
      style="--width: 14px;"
    >
      <path d="M7.21191 2.18994V12.5839" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M2.01562 7.38696H12.4096" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  

                    </span>
                  </button>
                  <div id="accordion-toggle-content-faq_4" class="accordion-toggle-content">
                    <div class="faq-block__details-content rte">
                      <h6>Need to Cancel?</h6><p>Give us a 48-hour heads-up when life gets in the way! Cancel on time and we'll hook you up with a full credit for your next session. Just remember, we can't issue refunds or credits for last-minute cancellations (under 48 hours)—those courts are hot property!</p><h6>No-Shows</h6><p>Ghosting the courts? Not cool! If you're a no-show, your booking fee takes the hit. Multiple vanishing acts might mean you'll miss out on future pickle fun. We want to keep our community vibe strong and courts filled with players ready to bring their A-game!</p><h6>When Mother Nature Crashes the Party</h6><p>Typhoon days happen! If the weather turns sour, we've got your back with a reschedule option. We're all about keeping the good times rolling, even when the clouds roll in.</p><p>To reschedule, just follow the simple steps on our website. Thanks for helping us keep our pickle community thriving!</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div><div class="faq-accordion-item">
                  <button type="button" class="h5 accordion-toggle-btn" data-toggle="#accordion-toggle-content-faq_5">
                    Is there a waitlist for full sessions, and how does it work? 
                    <span class="toggle-svg button--primary">
                      
    <svg
      class="svg-icon icon-plus"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="14"
      height="14"
      viewBox="0 0 14 14"
      fill="none"
      style="--width: 14px;"
    >
      <path d="M7.21191 2.18994V12.5839" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M2.01562 7.38696H12.4096" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  

                    </span>
                  </button>
                  <div id="accordion-toggle-content-faq_5" class="accordion-toggle-content">
                    <div class="faq-block__details-content rte">
                      <p>Yes, if a session is full, you can opt to join the waitlist. Should a slot become available, you will be notified. It's a great way to still have a chance to play, especially for popular sessions. All available slots are filled on a first-come, first-serve basis, so being on the waitlist keeps you in the running for any last-minute openings.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div><div class="faq-accordion-item">
                  <button type="button" class="h5 accordion-toggle-btn" data-toggle="#accordion-toggle-content-faq_D9Taih">
                    FREE PARKING 
                    <span class="toggle-svg button--primary">
                      
    <svg
      class="svg-icon icon-plus"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="14"
      height="14"
      viewBox="0 0 14 14"
      fill="none"
      style="--width: 14px;"
    >
      <path d="M7.21191 2.18994V12.5839" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M2.01562 7.38696H12.4096" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  

                    </span>
                  </button>
